,"synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The Bemaraha woolly lemur (Avahi cleesei), also known as Cleese's woolly lemur, is a species of woolly lemur native to western Madagascar, named after John Cleese. The first scientist to discover the species named it after Cleese, star of Monty Python, mainly because of Cleese's fondness for lemurs, as shown in Operation Lemur with John Cleese and Fierce Creatures, and his efforts at protecting and preserving them.","revisionId":1366332141,"title":"Bemaraha woolly lemur","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bemaraha_woolly_lemur","wikidataId":"Q1099688"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Gelada","source":"The IUCN Red List of Threatened Species"},{"language":"en","name":"obscurus","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Gelada Baboon","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Southern Gelada","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Bleeding-heart Monkey","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Southern Gelada (obscurus)","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Theropithecus gelada","confidence":99,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Theropithecus gelada (Rüppell, 1835)","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2436553},"ottId":741053,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Theropithecus gelada","synonyms":["Macacus gelada"],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The gelada (Theropithecus gelada, Amharic: ጭላዳ, romanized: č̣əlada, Oromo: Jaldeessa daabee), sometimes called the bleeding-heart monkey or the gelada baboon, is a species of Old World monkey found only in the Ethiopian Highlands, living at elevations of 1,800–4,400 m (5,900–14,400 ft) above sea level. It is the only living member of the genus Theropithecus, a name derived from the Greek root words for \"beast-ape\" (θηρο-πίθηκος : thēro-píthēkos).","revisionId":1343761319,"title":"Gelada","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gelada","wikidataId":"Q194080"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Golden Plovers And Bl